  "oneLinerQuestion": "Generate all combinations of n pairs of well-formed parentheses.",
  "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/generate-parentheses/",
  "explanation": "We build valid strings recursively using backtracking. An open parenthesis can be added if the count is under n, and a closing parenthesis can only be added if it does not exceed the count of currently open parentheses.",
  "pseudoCode": "FUNCTION generateParenthesis(n):\n    res = []\n    FUNCTION backtrack(openCount, closeCount, current):\n        IF LENGTH(current) == 2 * n THEN APPEND current TO res; RETURN\n        IF openCount < n THEN backtrack(openCount + 1, closeCount, current + '(')\n        IF closeCount < openCount THEN backtrack(openCount, closeCount + 1, current + ')')\n    END FUNCTION\n    backtrack(0, 0, '')\n    RETURN res\nEND FUNCTION",
  "renderType": "tree_backtrack",
